    "title": "Toyota Built a V12 Limo With Back-Seat Touchscreens, and One Is Live on BaT - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Elizabeth Puckett ,\n8 hours ago\nToyota built exactly one production V12, and it put it in a chauffeur car that Americans were never supposed to see. That's the second-generation Century, and this 2000 Toyota Century on Bring a Trailer is worth a look for one reason: it has the Dual Electro Multi-Vision package, a factory option that put touchscreens in the dash and in the back seat before most people owned a cell phone with a color screen. The auction is no reserve and ends Saturday, October 31 at 2:39 p.m. ET. The bid sat at $2,000 when we checked.\nRead full article",
